{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadLinkScaffold","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadLinkScaffold","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadChainVolume","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ExponentialGrowthRate"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_log_norm_whiteheadLinkKashaev_of_majorant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_log_norm_whiteheadLinkKashaev_of_majorant","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadLinkScaffold.lean#L141-L231","doc":"**Conditional volume limit for the Whitehead link (derived, not\naxiomatised).**  Given the Lemma-4 class AND the majorant volume rate\n(the open 2D brick W6, bean qou-oiv6), the Whitehead-link Kashaev\nmodulus obeys the volume conjecture:\n`(2π/N)·log ‖J_N‖ → 4·Cl₂(π/2) = 4G = Vol(L5a1)`.\n\n**The squeeze is no longer hand-rolled.**  It is\n`QOU.MathlibExt.tendsto_log_div_of_sandwich` — *a sub-exponential sandwich\ndoes not move an exponential growth rate* — instantiated at\n\n    m N = majorant N / N^p ,   S N = ‖J_N‖ ,   c N = N^p ,\n\nfor which `m ≤ S` is exactly `VdVWhiteheadLemma4.phase_cost` and\n`S ≤ c·m` is exactly the sorry-free triangle bound\n`norm_whiteheadLinkKashaev_le`.  That is the whole content of the\nconditional: the class supplies one inequality, the triangle bound the\nother, and the shared lemma does the analysis.\n\nNote the direction.  The shared lemma is stated knowing the *small* side's\nrate and concluding about the *large* one; here it is the large side\n(`majorant`) whose rate is known.  Dividing the known side by `N^p` is what\nputs it in the lemma's `m` slot — and it costs nothing precisely because\n`log(N^p)/N → 0`, which is the same sub-exponentiality the lemma's `c`\nslot wants.  Getting this backwards (trying `m = ‖J_N‖`) asks for the rate\nthat is open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VdVWhiteheadLemma4.phase_cost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VdVWhiteheadLemma4.phase_cost","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadLinkScaffold.lean#L138-L138","doc":"The majorant exceeds the modulus by at most `N^p` for some fixed `p`,\neventually in `N` — phases cost polynomially, never exponentially. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VdVWhiteheadLemma4.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VdVWhiteheadLemma4.mk","kind":"ctor","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadLinkScaffold.lean#L135-L135","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VdVWhiteheadLemma4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VdVWhiteheadLemma4","kind":"class","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadLinkScaffold.lean#L127-L139","doc":"**vdV Lemma 4, axiomatised as a primary conjecture class** (§3b-tax; no\ninstance is provided — this is the open analytic input).  Content: the\nFresnel phases of the `b = 1` outer sum cost at most a fixed power of\n`N` — the stationary-phase constant is nonzero, so modulus and majorant\nshare their exponential growth.  This is the analytic essence of\nvan der Veen's Lemma 4 (Gaussian → erfc, arXiv:math/0611181 §3); a\nfuture sorry-free discharge would formalize that argument.\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] library/arxiv-math-0611181v2/0611181v2.pdf, Lemma 4 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.norm_whiteheadLinkKashaev_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.norm_whiteheadLinkKashaev_le","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadLinkScaffold.lean#L109-L125","doc":"**The triangle bound (sorry-free)** — the upper half of the future\n`b = 1` squeeze: `‖J_N‖ ≤ majorant N`.  The global `φ_N` and each\n`χ_{N,n}^{-1}` are unimodular, the inner sums are positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadLinkMajorant_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadLinkMajorant_pos","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadLinkScaffold.lean#L96-L107","doc":"The majorant is strictly positive for `N ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadLink_inner_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadLink_inner_pos","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadLinkScaffold.lean#L86-L94","doc":"Each inner sum is strictly positive (`n ≤ N−1` leaves at least the\n`k = 0` term, and every term is an in-grid positive `S_{n,k}`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadLinkMajorant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadLinkMajorant","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadLinkScaffold.lean#L81-L84","doc":"The positive majorant: the same double sum with the phases dropped. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadLinkKashaev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadLinkKashaev","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadLinkScaffold.lean#L73-L79","doc":"The `b = 1` Whitehead-link Lemma-1 sum at the Kashaev point (faithful\ntranscription; `φ_N = exp((N−1)πi/N)` for `c+d = 1`, inner sums are the\npositive `S_{n,k}` of the chain file with the `M`-slot at `n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadLinkPhase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadLinkPhase","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadLinkScaffold.lean#L67-L71","doc":"The Fresnel phase `χ_{N,n}^{-1} = exp(−n(n+1−N)πi/(2N))` of vdV\nLemma 1 at exponent `4a−c+d = −1` (the Whitehead link `W_{0,1,1,0}`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}